@startuml predecode_feedback
title Decoded instruction -> dynamic prediction binding -> target consumption
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

legend left
  |= Prefix |= Meaning |
  | [E] | Existing gem5 call, return, or signal |
  | [N] | Proposed interface or integration hook |
  | [A] | Algorithm step / private plumbing, not a C++ method |
  Conditional outcomes are resolved by execution, not by predecode.
endlegend

participant Fetch
participant "ISA decoder" as Decoder
participant "O3 CPU" as CPU
participant "DynInst / fetchQueue" as Inst
participant BAC
participant Gem5BpuBridge as Bridge
participant IBPU
participant PredictionLedger as Ledger
participant BlockFetchEngine as Engine
participant FTQ
participant "O3 time buffers" as TB

note over Fetch, FTQ
  Entry condition: live FTQ target, active BlockCursor, enough bytes for the
  next instruction, and fetchWidth / fetchQueue capacity. See fetch_blocks_merge.
  This is Fetch-stage ISA decoding; it occurs before the O3 Decode stage.
end note

Fetch -> Decoder : [E] decode(this_pc), or fetch macro/ROM microop
Decoder --> Fetch : [E] StaticInst
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] buildInst(tid, staticInst, macroop, this_pc, next_pc, true)
Fetch -> CPU : [E] getAndIncrementInstSeq()
CPU --> Fetch : [E] InstSeqNum
Fetch -> Inst : [E] construct DynInst with actual PC / StaticInst
Fetch -> CPU : [E] addInst(instruction)
Fetch -> Inst : [E] fetchQueue[tid].push_back(instruction)
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] ppFetch->notify(); numInst++; set fetchTick
Fetch -> BAC : [E] updatePC(instruction, next_pc, curFT)

note over Fetch, Bridge
  In legacy mode, BAC::updatePC calls updatePreDecode only for controls.
  In IBPU mode, hook every decoded instruction to detect phantom CFIs too.
  Keep this call site; dispatch inside BAC according to selected mode.
  Required new plumbing: expose Fetch's active BlockCursor to BAC.
  The existing updatePC(inst, pc, ft) signature does not carry a cursor.
end note

BAC -> Bridge : [N] bindAndPredict(inst, activeCursor)
Bridge -> Bridge : [A] find CFI by dynamic key + blockIndex + actual PC;
Bridge -> Bridge : [A] build PredecodeFeedback, including matchedCfi if any
Bridge -> IBPU : [N] onPredecodeFeedback(fb)
IBPU -> Ledger : [N] bind(fb)
alt decoded control matches a predicted CFI
    Ledger -> Ledger : [A] bind instSeq to BranchRef(key, blockIndex, cfiId)
    Ledger -> Ledger : [A] retain model history / lookup metadata for that query
    Ledger --> IBPU : [N] PredictionBinding(branch, taken, nextPC, needsRepair)
else decoded control missing from prediction
    Ledger -> Ledger : [A] allocate dynamic CFI identity / history binding
    Ledger -> Ledger : [A] retain real type and length; mark missing prediction
    Ledger --> IBPU : [N] provisional binding requiring model fallback
    IBPU -> IBPU : [A] choose fallback prediction and required speculative-history repair
    note over IBPU, Ledger
      Missing-CFI policy belongs to the selected model.
      Existing BAC uses a not-taken placeholder for this common case;
      its taken-history assumption cannot be imposed on all IBPU models.
      If new history affects later predictions, recover/recompute that suffix.
    end note
else predicted CFI is a normal instruction, or type/length mismatch
    Ledger -> Ledger : [A] mark stale metadata; identify invalid speculative suffix
    Ledger --> IBPU : [N] binding with needsRepair = true and corrected fetch choice
else ordinary non-control instruction with no matching CFI
    Ledger --> IBPU : [N] no BranchRef; sequential nextPC; taken = false
end
IBPU --> Bridge : [N] PredictionBinding
note over Bridge, Ledger
  PC, instruction identity/type/length and direct static targets become known.
  No real conditional direction or indirect target is learned here.
  CFI.isPrediction = false is NOT proof of an executed branch outcome.
  Same PC in another block/loop iteration still has a different binding.
  Macroop/microop handling must preserve full PCState and last-uop boundaries.
end note

Bridge -> Bridge : [A] combine binding with block limits / next block PC
Bridge --> BAC : [N] FetchDecision(nextPC, predictedTaken,\nblockDone, targetDone, needsRepair)

alt decision requires metadata / path repair
    BAC -> Bridge : [A] record exact pending cut and corrected fetch choice
    Bridge -> Bridge : [A] retain key / block / instruction boundary and restartPC
    note over Fetch, FTQ
      Detect and record repair here; do not call onRecovery yet.
      Fetch will stop affected consumption and signal the existing BAC route.
      Shared sidecar state preserves the exact cut across fetchToBacDelay.
      Do not also train this event as an execute misprediction.
      Corrected nextPC is sequential or statically derived where possible;
      unresolved conditional / indirect choices remain predictions.
    end note
end

opt decoded instruction closes this block, with no repair already pending
    BAC -> Bridge : [N] finishBlock(activeCursor)
    Bridge -> Bridge : [A] audit predicted CFI positions not matched during decode
    alt leftover phantom CFI / incompatible byte boundary
        Bridge -> Bridge : [A] record exact pending cut / corrected fetch choice
        note over BAC, Bridge
          finishBlock returns void in the class contract.
          This audit records shared repair state before normal consumption;
          it cannot silently return an unreported new FetchDecision.
          Use the same delayed repair path as bindAndPredict.
          Neither detection site calls onRecovery immediately.
          Final microop must complete before declaring a block finished.
        end note
    else block metadata consistent
        Bridge -> Bridge : [A] close this block; keep target if later blocks remain
    end
end

BAC -> BAC : [A] finalize next_pc / predictedTaken from binding or pending correction
BAC -> Inst : [E] setPredTarg(next_pc)
BAC -> Inst : [E] setPredTaken(predictedTaken)
BAC -> BAC : [A] clear curFT only if whole target done or marked unusable by repair
BAC --> Fetch : [E] return predictedTaken
Fetch -> Fetch : [E] set(this_pc, next_pc); update macroop / byte offset state
alt a pending repair supplies an exact cancellation cut
    Fetch -> Engine : [N] invalidateYounger(cut)
    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] retain surviving prefix; stop consuming affected target bytes
    note over Fetch, BAC
      The boolean updatePC return cannot carry a recovery cut.
      Share repair state through the BAC/Fetch integration plumbing.
      Do not advance an invalidated target cursor or resume it before repair.
    end note
else current cursor still valid
    Fetch -> Engine : [N] advance(nextPC, decodedBytes)
end

alt no pending repair, current block ends and more valid blocks remain
    Fetch -> Engine : [N] blockDone() / targetDone()
    Engine --> Fetch : [N] block done, target not done
    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] continue at next block if bytes and bandwidth allow
    note over Fetch, Engine
      Modify legacy predictedBranch loop-stop and flat inRange checks.
      A taken exit may continue into the next block of the SAME target.
      Enforce block/taken bandwidth limits; no FTQ pop at this transition.
      Preserve true PC and discard no surviving instruction bytes.
    end note
else whole target consumed without pending repair
    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] retain head key / ownership state across popHead()
    Fetch -> FTQ : [E] popHead(tid), now once per whole target
    FTQ --> Fetch : [E] bool success
    alt pop succeeded
        Fetch -> BAC : [A] forward consumed key through BAC's owned bridge
        BAC -> Bridge : [A] forward consumed key
        Bridge -> IBPU : [N] onTargetConsumed(key)
        IBPU -> Ledger : [N] markFetchConsumed(key)
        note over IBPU, Ledger
          This releases fetch ownership, not all prediction metadata.
          Preserve InstSeqNum bindings and history until commit/recovery
          and all slow-stage users finish. FTQ pop is not training.
          The class has no named BAC/bridge consumed-forwarding helper yet.
        end note
        opt another target is ready and bandwidth permits
            Fetch -> FTQ : [E] readHead(tid)
            FTQ --> Fetch : [E] next FetchTargetPtr
            Fetch -> Engine : [N] begin(nextFT)
        end
    else pop failed
        Fetch -> Fetch : [A] record pending repair; stop affected consumption
        Fetch -> Engine : [N] invalidateYounger(cut)
        note right of FTQ
          Legacy false has two meanings: leftover history prevents removal,
          but a Locked head is removed and still returns false.
          If retained: recovery owns that queued payload's cleanup.
          If already removed: retain its key/metadata through the sidecar;
          release fetch ownership once, with no second FTQ pop.
          Do not report this canceled target as normally consumed.
        end note
    end
else repair pending for current target
    Fetch -> Fetch : [A] stop consuming canceled bytes; retain repair sidecar
end

opt a pending repair has not already been signaled
    Fetch -> Fetch : [E] bacResteer(restartPC, tid)
    Fetch -> TB : [E] write fetchInfo.squash = true; nextPC = restartPC
    Fetch -> FTQ : [E] invalidate(tid)
    Fetch -> BAC : [A] forward exact repair sidecar through BAC's bridge plumbing
    BAC -> Bridge : [A] retain pending cut / restartPC and payload ownership
    note over Fetch, Bridge
      Existing FetchComm carries squash and nextPC only.
      Add a sidecar or small signal extension for the dynamic cut.
      While pending, block affected admission and fetch consumption;
      do not erase the surviving instruction's binding or metadata.
    end note
end

note over Fetch, Inst
  buildInst enqueued the DynInst BEFORE BAC::updatePC above.
  The same object's prediction fields are finalized before publication.
  The current DynInst and valid older prefix may publish normally.
  Fetch::tick drains surviving fetchQueue entries toDecode, up to decodeWidth.
  No direct call to the Decode stage is made here.
end note

... fetchToBacDelay, if a repair was signaled ...
ref over Fetch, BAC, Bridge, IBPU
  backend_recovery.puml: Fetch requests a BAC resteer
  BAC receives fetchInfo after older Commit/Decode recovery arbitration.
  forwardFeedback applies onRecovery(FetchRepair, cut, restartPC) exactly once,
  or an older recovery supersedes and discards this pending request.
  Only here restore model history and remove the invalid frontend suffix.
  resolvedOutcome is absent for this predecode repair.
end ref

note over Fetch, FTQ
  Existing anchors: src/cpu/o3/fetch.cc buildInst:1005, fetch:1058,
  buildInst call:1276, BAC::updatePC call:1291, popHead:1339,
  time-buffer publication:891. src/cpu/o3/bac.cc
  updatePreDecode:764, updatePC:904; src/cpu/o3/ftq.cc popHead:238.
  New signatures are from research/uml/class/class_diagram_v2.puml.
end note
@enduml
